course: dictionary
lesson: 9468
title: Two meanings of starving
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentences around them tell you which meaning is right. Look for clues in the words near the word you don't know. In «Mum I'm starving, I haven't eaten in like a hundred years», Leo is shouting after school, and we learn he had lunch at twelve. That clue tells you he means he is really hungry.
explain: Starving has two meanings. The first is serious: very ill or dying because there has been no food for a long time, as in people starving in a famine. The second is informal, and it is what most people say: very hungry, as in «I'm starving!» before dinner.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «I'm really hungry» fits Leo, because he has eaten today. The serious meaning does not fit, because Leo would not be dying after a lunch at twelve. Always ask: does this meaning make sense with the clues around it?
explain: People say «I'm starving» to make hunger sound bigger than it is. That is a kind of exaggeration. The serious meaning is never a joke: people who are truly starving need food and help quickly.
fact: Starving can mean very ill or dying because of having no food for a long time.
fact: Informally, starving means very hungry, as in «I'm starving!»
fact: Starving to death means dying because there is no food.
fact: In geography and history, starving describes people in a famine, and charities help them.
fact: In science, living things need food to survive, which is why the serious meaning of starving matters.
exercise: «Mum I'm starving, I haven't eaten in like a hundred years.» What does starving mean in this sentence? | Very cold after playing outside | Very tired after a long day | Very ill and dying | *Very hungry, the informal meaning
exercise: In a geography lesson, charities help people who are starving in a famine. What does starving mean here? | Bored of school | Very hungry before dinner | *Very ill or dying because they have no food for a long time | Full up after a big meal
exercise: Leo says he hasn't eaten in a hundred years, but he had lunch at twelve. What clue shows he is not really starving? | It is after school | He bursts in after school | *He had lunch at twelve, so he has eaten recently | He is shouting loudly
test: «Starving animals» in a science lesson means what? | Animals that are very hungry before their dinner, so they are fine | *Animals that have had no food for a long time and are in danger | Animals that like to eat a lot | Animals that are full and sleeping
test: Which phrase shows the serious meaning of starving? | *starving to death | starving at school | starving for a biscuit | I'm starving before dinner
exam: Nadia says «I'm starving» but she just had toast. Why is she using the informal meaning? | Because she is in a famine | Because she is ill and dying | Because she has had no food for weeks | *Because she means she is very hungry
